.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MKDIR 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mkdir
.Nd make directories
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl pv
.Op Fl m Ar mode
.Ar directory_name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes each
.Ar directory_name ,
in the order given, with mode 0777 less the
.Xr umask 2 .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl m Ar mode
Give each directory made exactly
.Ar mode ,
octal or symbolic as for
.Xr chmod 1 ;
a symbolic mode starts from
.Li a=rwx ,
so that
.Li g-w
means 0757 less the umask's other bits.
Set-ID and sticky bits are kept.
.It Fl p
Make any missing parent directories first, each with the umask's mode plus
the owner's write and search permission, and don't complain about a
directory that already exists.
.Fl m
applies only to the last component.
.It Fl v
Write the name of each directory made, parents too.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Make a tree in one go, private to its owner at the end:
.Dl mkdir -p -m 700 src/oxidebsd/private
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr chmod 1 ,
.Xr rmdir 1 ,
.Xr mkdir 2 ,
.Xr umask 2
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 ;
.Fl v
is an extension, as on the BSDs.
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v1 .
